he Twelfth Dynasty under Senusret III and Amenemhat III.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/khusrau-malik"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/khusrau-malik.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Khusrau Malik</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Khusrau Malik was the last sultan of the Ghaznavid dynasty, ruling from Lahore over the Ghaznavid lands in the Punjab from 1160.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/khusrau-shah"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/khusrau-shah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Khusrau Shah</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Khusrau Shah was a sultan of the Ghaznavid dynasty and son of Bahram Shah, reigning from 1157 to 1160.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/khust"><span class="enc-name">Khust</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Khust is a town in Zakarpattia Oblast in western Ukraine, on the Tysa river below the ruins of a medieval castle.</span></a></li></ul>
